A||||5||Drapes85Fiero||troubleshooting help||||5||
Z||000000||Drapes85Fiero||05-24-2000||12:32 AM||||  I need some help I have a light problem the low beams don't work but the brights do I need to know if some one could take a measurement form the headlight wires (Green,Tan,Black ) to ground with the headlights on and with them off.  The way I see it is that my green wire is shorted to ground when power is applied causeing my problem.  whats the easiest way of fixing this with out taking out the entire harness?  Thanks I know I sound stupid but I just need a second opinion.<BR>Dave||||reg||5
Z||000001||Gold-86SE||05-24-2000||10:08 AM||||<BR>Without trying to sound like an idiot, are you sure that the low beam are not blown.  All you may need is a simple replacement of the headlights.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Drapes85Fiero||05-24-2000||06:42 PM||||I would love to check but how can you tell if the low beams are blown?  Thanks for the help!<BR>Dave||||reg||5
Z||000003||DRH||05-24-2000||07:02 PM||||You didn't mention the high beams not working so I assume they do.<P>If a headlight wire was shorted dead to ground you would blow a fusible link somewhere. I'm pretty sure the highs work off the same power source so I don't think that is your problem. <P>Measure with a voltmetter or a 12V test light at the connector to the headlight. I'm not sure of the color coding but I believe black is ground. You should have approx 12V (or a lit test light) between either green or tan and black when lights are on low and between the other color and black when on high. If you are getting 12 volts to the low beam side of the light and it's not coming on, then the bulb is bad.<P>If you're not getting power the next suspect would be the dimmer switch.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Drapes85Fiero||05-24-2000||07:23 PM||||OK I went and did that I have 12v on my brights and 0 on my low beams I swaped out the dimmer switch with 2 other ones and still nothing.  any other suggestions thanks for all the help so far!!!<BR>Dave||||reg||1
Z||000005||DRH||05-25-2000||11:21 AM||||I looked at the wiring diagram in the Haynes manual last night. Black is ground, Tan is low beam and Light Green is high beam. The dimmer switch has a Yellow wire as input and switches between the Tan and Green. Confirm you have power at the Yellow and Tan wire coming from the dimmer switch. Check for power on the Tan wire at the left headlight. Check the connector closely to make sure the wires haven't come loose from the terminal. If you have power at the dimmer switch and not at the light, check wire close to light to see if it somehow got broken (internally) with headlight going up and down. Next check the connector where it comes thru from the passenger compartment. <P>Check all wire to terminal connections closely. This is the most likely place to loose connection. Last resort is to start tracing the wire thru the harness.<P>Good luck.<P>||||reg||1
